    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T21:54:24Z",
    "body": "Priority raised P3 -> P1 (issue-worker-high, 2026-11-13).\n\nReasoning, by the AGENTS.md table (\"P1: unsafe or wrong output: a gouge or collision that passes\"): the Bore op posts a program that verifies `ok` with no finding, yet on a through hole it frees a Ø66 mm disc (the ring and the centre slot leave an annulus with no material joining it to the wall) at the last level. A loose core under a spinning 4 mm end mill is thrown or wedged against the tool - a crash hazard in front of the operator, after the verifier passed it. That is unsafe output that passes, not a wrong-but-safe result with a workaround. On a blind hole the same ride leaves an uncut island and still says `ok`: wrong output that passes. Both are P1 shape; the hand workaround (delete the hole from the list) only helps a user who noticed.\n\nThe work stays effort:high: the fix is a refusal law in the motion kernel plus the detect-holes rule in app, with MCP/UI parity.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
